#: 319f4c02de7848e1b27e260940f77555
msgid ""
"And even more, we can also sort along a specific dimension without "
"needing to even specify any dimension nor axis. For example, to sort "
"along the time dimension using the means of the `DataArray` we can do:"
msgstr ""

#: ../sphinx_source/blog/posts/2023/xarray_intro.ipynb:100002
#: 5dca356fb8a9458cbfc62a448cca73c1
msgid ""
"As the `time_means` `DataArray` has a single dimension and it is named "
"`time`, `.sortby` sorts along that dimension."
msgstr ""

#: ../sphinx_source/blog/posts/2023/xarray_intro.ipynb:100004
#: 8c92ee981aff4ce687b52ad344109d26
msgid ""
"Having this information also allows xarray to perform automatic "
"broadcasting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../sphinx_source/blog/posts/2023/xarray_intro.ipynb:120002
#: f0c741b7d9524f72ac62385135c7f68e
msgid ""
"Still, for the most part, `DataArray`s are interchangeable with ndarrays,"
" even for functions that don't support `DataArray`s explicitly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../sphinx_source/blog/posts/2023/xarray_intro.ipynb:140002
#: ed38b3c4a6e14d0fb97e89e9906ceb02
msgid ""
"It is possible to convert a `DataArray` to an ndarray using `da.values` "
"but as we have just seen, very often it is not necessary."
